3) ✅ Scheduled Task \eMatch Automation\RunEMatchDesktop precisa apontar pra ESTE BAT

Você perguntou “o que coloco nesse bat run?” ✅
Coloque esse arquivo inteiro em:

D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\run-ematch-command.bat
D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\run-ematch-command.bat (INTEIRO)
@echo off
setlocal EnableExtensions EnableDelayedExpansion

rem ============================================================
rem Generic runner for eMatch Desktop execution via Katalon Engine
rem Reads: D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\run-context.properties
rem Writes results into WORKSPACE\Reports and a marker file
rem ============================================================

set "CTX=D:\Projects\eMatchStarters\run-context.properties"
if not exist "%CTX%" (
  echo [ERROR] Missing context file: %CTX%
  exit /b 10
)

rem Read properties
for /f "usebackq tokens=1,* delims==" %%A in ("%CTX%") do (
  set "K=%%A"
  set "V=%%B"
  if /I "!K!"=="WORKSPACE"      set "WORKSPACE=!V!"
  if /I "!K!"=="KATALON_EXE"    set "KATALON_EXE=!V!"
  if /I "!K!"=="PROJECT_FILE"   set "PROJECT_FILE=!V!"
  if /I "!K!"=="SUITE_PATH"     set "SUITE_PATH=!V!"
)

if "%WORKSPACE%"=="" (
  echo [ERROR] WORKSPACE not set in %CTX%
  exit /b 11
)

if "%KATALON_EXE%"=="" (
  echo [ERROR] KATALON_EXE not set in %CTX%
  exit /b 12
)

if "%PROJECT_FILE%"=="" (
  echo [ERROR] PROJECT_FILE not set in %CTX%
  exit /b 13
)

if "%SUITE_PATH%"=="" (
  echo [ERROR] SUITE_PATH not set in %CTX%
  exit /b 14
)

rem Ensure Reports folder
if not exist "%WORKSPACE%\Reports" mkdir "%WORKSPACE%\Reports" >nul 2>nul

echo ============================================================
echo RUNNING KATALON
echo WORKSPACE    : %WORKSPACE%
echo KATALON_EXE  : %KATALON_EXE%
echo PROJECT_FILE : %PROJECT_FILE%
echo SUITE_PATH   : %SUITE_PATH%
echo ============================================================

pushd "%WORKSPACE%"

"%KATALON_EXE%" ^
  -noSplash ^
  -runMode=console ^
  -projectPath="%WORKSPACE%\%PROJECT_FILE%" ^
  -retry=0 ^
  -testSuitePath="%SUITE_PATH%" ^
  -browserType="Windows" ^
  -reportFolder="Reports" ^
  -reportFileName="report"

set "EC=%ERRORLEVEL%"

echo %EC%> "%WORKSPACE%\Reports\_jenkins_task_exitcode.txt"

popd

echo ============================================================
echo KATALON FINISHED. EXITCODE=%EC%
echo Marker file: %WORKSPACE%\Reports\_jenkins_task_exitcode.txt
echo ============================================================

exit /b %EC%
4) ✅ O Jenkins precisa passar o “contexto” pro task (SEM inventar ambiente)

Como você disse: quem decide REC/PRD e quando abre/fecha é o teste de login, não o Jenkins ✅
Então o Jenkins só precisa garantir:

✅ task roda no desktop certo (Task Scheduler)
✅ task sabe o workspace + suite que vai rodar

Pra isso, antes de rodar schtasks, o Jenkinsfile já tem Prepare Artifacts.
Agora você só precisa garantir que ele escreve o run-context.properties correto.

Se você quiser que o Jenkinsfile já escreva (recomendado), adicione isso no stage Prepare Artifacts (dentro do Jenkinsfile acima), substituindo o bloco simples por este:

stage('Prepare Artifacts') {
  writeFile file: 'D:\\Projects\\eMatchStarters\\run-context.properties', text: """
WORKSPACE=${pwd()}
KATALON_EXE=C:\\Users\\ladgi5appjenkins\\Documents\\Katalon_Studio_Engine_Windows_64-8.1.0\\katalonc.exe
PROJECT_FILE=eMatch POC.prj
SUITE_PATH=Test Suites/Archive Mode/Archive Mode Collection
""".trim()

  bat 'if not exist "Reports" mkdir "Reports"'
}

